    "body": "## Problem\n\nThree agents share this monorepo, and each is told about every pull request whatever it touches. Issues already carry an area label, but pull requests carry none, so nothing can narrow a pull request down to the agents it concerns.\n\n## Change\n\n- A `label-areas` job in `ci.yml` applies `area:record`, `area:web` and `area:agent` from the paths a pull request changes, as mapped in `.github/labeler.yml`. On each push it also removes an area the pull request no longer touches (`sync-labels: true`).\n- Every package under `packages/` is mapped. `acp-transcripts` goes to `area:agent`, and the label's description now says so.\n- The three labels were renamed from `area: record` / `area: web` / `area: agent`, with the space removed. Every issue kept its label: 66 / 25 / 36 before and after.\n\nagent-bus will add a `labels/<label>` subscription, so an agent can subscribe to the areas it works on.\n\n## Controls\n\n- `label-areas` is a job in the existing workflow, not a separate one. Each workflow run is its own check suite, so a separate workflow would send another notification on every push.\n- `run-ci-build` doesn't depend on it, so labelling never gates a merge.\n- A change outside `packages/` (root `tests/`, `scripts/`, `docs/`, `.github/`) gets no area. This pull request is one of those.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XEC2HFFH318qFYCQ1M9LFK",
